      "math_academy_id": "q-105137",
      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are sets. If $|X|=2$ and $|Y|=6,$ then $|P(X)|+|P(Y)|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S$, $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ \n\nIn this case, $|X|=2$ and $|Y|=6,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(X)|+|P(Y)| & ={2}^{|X|}+{2}^{|Y|} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{2}^{6} \\\\  & =4+64 \\\\  & =68.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
